    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 all 32 tests pass, including the new `Cp21Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the audit-on-create requirement for `POST /api/owners`:\n\n1. **New function class** `AuditOwnerCreated.java` \u2014 emits an info line via the SLF4J logger named `AUDIT`, containing the owner id, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate`:\n   ```\n   INFO  AUDIT - owner created id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-08-14\n   ```\n\n2. **Wired it into the pipeline** in `owners.POST.yml` as a new `audit` step between `save` and `respond` \u2014 so it runs only after a successful save (when the id is assigned) and under the same transaction governance as its neighbors, reading the built `Owner` via `@Val`.\n\nThe step fires only on the success path (a failed create throws an escalation before reaching `save`/`audit`), matching \"on successful create.\" The `LocalDate` logged via `{}` renders as ISO `yyyy-MM-dd`, matching the JSON `registrationDate` text the test asserts against.",
